#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""omarchy-mic-fx: the helper behind the io.github.codemonkey76.micfx Omarchy widget.

Puts a processed copy of a microphone in front of it -- input gain, high-pass,
RNNoise noise suppression, gate, compressor, limiter -- as a virtual source
that every app (Zoom, Teams, browsers) can record from. The chain is a
PipeWire filter-chain hosted by its own PipeWire client under a systemd user
service, the way Omarchy hosts its speaker tuning, so switching it on and off
never restarts the audio daemon.

  omarchy-mic-fx status                  everything the widget shows, as JSON
  omarchy-mic-fx on [--keep-default]     start it and make it the default input
  omarchy-mic-fx off                     stop it and give the default input back
  omarchy-mic-fx default                 make the running chain the default input
  omarchy-mic-fx set KEY VALUE           change one setting, live and saved
  omarchy-mic-fx device NAME             process a different input device
  omarchy-mic-fx devices                 input devices that can be processed
  omarchy-mic-fx reset                   back to the default settings
  omarchy-mic-fx render                  print the PipeWire config it would use
  omarchy-mic-fx uninstall               stop it and remove its service and config
  omarchy-mic-fx calibrate PHASE SECS    record one wizard phase: quiet, speech or typing
  omarchy-mic-fx calibrate solve         settings suggested by the recorded phases
  omarchy-mic-fx calibrate apply         apply those suggestions
  omarchy-mic-fx calibrate preview       mix the typing over the talking, before and after the chain
  omarchy-mic-fx calibrate play WHICH    play that preview: before or after
  omarchy-mic-fx calibrate clear         delete the wizard's audio clips

Files it writes are opened without following symlinks and replaced
atomically, so a planted link can't redirect them. The wizard's talking and
typing clips live only in the memory-backed runtime directory, for the
preview, and are deleted when the wizard closes.
"""

